<DIV CLASS="title2">Rates</DIV>

<BLOCKQUOTE>
The Rates tab will display the products that you just selected in a table.  If you are applying the same <CFOUTPUT>#Application.RebateLabel#</CFOUTPUT> or net price to all the products, click the box in the upper left-hand corner of the table (orange bar).  This will automatically select all the items in the table.  Enter the <CFOUTPUT>#Application.RebateLabel#</CFOUTPUT> or net price amount in the Rate window.  After entering the correct amount, click on the “Apply” button.  The table will subsequently be filled in with that rate.  If your contract has different rate levels for different products, you will have to apply the rates in batches.  To do this, select the desired products by putting a check mark in the corresponding box to the left of the descriptor.  Enter the rate amount in the Rate window and click the “Apply” button.  Uncheck the boxes after the correct rate appears for those products.  Check the next batch of products and apply the different rate and continue this process until all the products have a <CFOUTPUT>#Application.RebateLabel#</CFOUTPUT> or net price associated with them.  If all the products have a different rate, it is easiest to directly input the rate in the box on the right side of the table that corresponds to each product.  You may also change the unit of measure if necessary by using the mini drop down menus on each product line.  Click the “Save” button.
</BLOCKQUOTE>